{"key": "Medical::Medical-97625b74", "time": "2026-10-09T15:24:27+00:00", "raw": {"candidates": [{"content": {"role": "model", "parts": [{"text": "The major subtypes of breast cancer include ductal carcinoma, lobular carcinoma, ductal carcinoma in situ, invasive breast cancer, metastatic breast cancer, and inflammatory breast cancer. Common symptoms include a breast lump, pain, nipple thickening or discharge, and changes in the size or shape of the breast. For inflammatory breast cancer, common symptoms include redness, swelling, feeling warm to the touch, a swollen nipple area, peau d’orange dimpling, skin thickening, edema, and erythema, often without a lump. The primary diagnostic methods include physical breast exams, imaging tests such as diagnostic and screening mammograms (2D digital mammograms or 3D tomosynthesis), MRIs, and ultrasounds. Additional diagnostic and staging methods include biopsies (such as needle biopsies or skin biopsies), blood tests, biomarker testing, genetic risk testing, and testing biopsy tissue for estrogen receptors, progesterone receptors, and HER2 receptor status.", "thoughtSignature": ""}]}, "finishReason": "STOP", "groundingMetadata": {"groundingChunks": [{"retrievedContext": {"uri": "Medical.txt", "title": "Medical.txt"}}, {"retrievedContext": {"uri": "Medical.txt", "title": "Medical.txt"}}, {"retrievedContext": {"uri": "Medical.txt", "title": "Medical.txt"}}], "groundingSupports": [{"segment": {"endIndex": 187, "text": "The major subtypes of breast cancer include ductal carcinoma, lobular carcinoma, ductal carcinoma in situ, invasive breast cancer, metastatic breast cancer, and inflammatory breast cancer"}, "groundingChunkIndices": [0, 1]}, {"segment": {"startIndex": 189, "endIndex": 312, "text": "Common symptoms include a breast lump, pain, nipple thickening or discharge, and changes in the size or shape of the breast"}, "groundingChunkIndices": [1]}, {"segment": {"startIndex": 314, "endIndex": 523, "text": "For inflammatory br